# Intentionally empty of host-level rules.
#
# A `www.mcpwatchman.com/* -> mcpwatchman.com/:splat` rule used to live here and
# it could never have worked: Cloudflare Pages matches a `_redirects` SOURCE as a
# PATH, not a full URL, so a rule whose source carries a hostname matches nothing.
# It was a silent no-op that read like a working redirect — worse than no rule,
# because it documented behaviour the platform does not implement.
#
# The apex is the only custom domain. Do not add `www` as a second one: two hosts
# answering identical content splits SEO and makes the HSTS/CSP story ambiguous.
# If www is ever wanted, the mechanism is a dashboard-side Bulk Redirect (or a
# redirect rule), which Cloudflare's own docs name for exactly this case — not a
# file in this repo.
